    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Soft-delete for owner deletion \u2014 implemented and green\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (both new acceptance tests: `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`).\n\n### What changed\n\n**Model \u2014 new `deleted` flag** (`model/Owner.java`)\n- Added `@Column(name = \"deleted\") private Boolean deleted = false;` with getter/setter. Defaulting to `false` in the field means a newly created owner (built via the mapper, which doesn't touch `deleted`) serializes as `deleted: false`.\n\n**Delete becomes soft** (`rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`)\n- Was `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`; now sets `owner.setDeleted(true)` and `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. The row is retained, and the `DELETE` pipeline still ends at `RespondWithNoContent` (204, a 2xx). `LoadOwner`/`GET` are unchanged and still return the retained owner, now with `deleted: true`.\n\n**Duplicate & identity checks ignore deleted owners**\n- `RejectDuplicateOwner.java` (the blocking household/identity check \u2192 409) and `DetectPossibleDuplicate.java` (the soft possible-duplicate flag) both now `continue` past any existing owner with `deleted == true`. So a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was soft-deleted.\n\n**Response DTO** (`resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it by name (no mapper edit needed).\n\n**Schema/seed data**\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` (the profile the tests use): added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE` to the `owners` table, and appended `FALSE` to the 10 positional seed inserts in `db/hsqldb/data.sql` so they still match the column count.\n- Added the `deleted` column to `db/mysql/schema.sql` and `db/postgres/schema.sql` for consistency (untested profiles; h2 uses `ddl-auto=update` and column-list inserts, so it needs no change).\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the pre-existing `db/mysql/data.sql` owner inserts already used a positional `VALUES` list with fewer values than the table's columns \u2014 that mismatch predates this change and isn't exercised by the test suite, so I left it alone.",
